        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Gerrymap you practice <strong>gerrymandering</strong>: drawing maps to decide the outcome of elections.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A state has four districts. In most elections, its vote is split equally. Each party should have two districts, right?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=289 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >NO! If we control redistricting, we pack the enemy party into just one district! This is the art of gerrymandering. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=286 /></span>It's not always so simple. A &quot;dummymander&quot; could give away all your seats in a bad election year. An overly conservative map could make further gains difficult. Also, some areas are very elastic, others are not!       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=298 /></span>The VRA says you have to create majority-minority districts in some states. As you play on the Democratic side in the campaign, this will force you to pack your voters! And expect to draw a lot of <strong>squiggly lines</strong>.       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Featuring</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A campaign mode with 10 states!</strong> Deal with the challenges Southern Democrats faced gerrymandering in 1990.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A sandbox mode with all 48 contiguous US states!</strong> 1976-2000 Presidential, Senate and Gubernatorial results for each state. Play around with it!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1990 census data: </strong>Race, sex, age, household income, and educational attainment! </p></li></ul>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Gerrymap you practice <strong>gerrymandering</strong>: drawing maps to decide the outcome of elections.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A state has four districts. In most elections, its vote is split equally. Each party should have two districts, right?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=289 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >NO! If we control redistricting, we pack the enemy party into just one district! This is the art of gerrymandering. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=286 /></span>It's not always so simple. A &quot;dummymander&quot; could give away all your seats in a bad election year. An overly conservative map could make further gains difficult. Also, some areas are very elastic, others are not!       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=298 /></span>The VRA says you have to create majority-minority districts in some states. As you play on the Democratic side in the campaign, this will force you to pack your voters! And expect to draw a lot of <strong>squiggly lines</strong>.       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Featuring</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A campaign mode with 10 states!</strong> Deal with the challenges Southern Democrats faced gerrymandering in 1990.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A sandbox mode with all 48 contiguous US states!</strong> 1976-2000 Presidential, Senate and Gubernatorial results for each state. Play around with it!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1990 census data: </strong>Race, sex, age, household income, and educational attainment! </p></li></ul>",
        "short_description": "Gerrymap is a puzzle game about gerrymandering. Win congressional seats for your party by drawing districts, using US Census data!",
